# City Context and Local-Time Rules (WatchAgent)

- Treat Ottawa, Toronto, and Vancouver as distinct monitoring contexts, not
  interchangeable labels.
- City-specific thresholds or events must have a clear project reason in README
  and at least one focused event-detection test.
- Keep temperature swing thresholds in `app/cities.py`; do not scatter duplicate
  city threshold constants through event logic.
- Time-window events must evaluate city-local time, not raw UTC hour, unless the
  README explicitly justifies a UTC-based interpretation.
- Ottawa-specific events should focus on winter surface conditions, freeze/thaw
  impacts, roads, sidewalks, pathways, or near-freezing wet conditions.
- Toronto-specific events should avoid claiming live TTC delay data. Phrase them
  as weather-risk proxies unless the project later integrates a real transit
  data source.
- Vancouver-specific events should preserve the coastal/rain/wind framing and
  avoid copying Ottawa or Toronto assumptions into Vancouver logic.
- Regional events must require readings from all monitored cities and a clear
  enough contrast to avoid declaring a winner during essentially similar
  conditions.
